   "source": [
    "# Hedging bot: delta hedging a book of APOs\n",
    "\n",
    "The book in `portfolios/example_book.yaml` holds three APOs with illustrative terms:\n",
    "\n",
    "| id | trade | pricing month | position |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| APO-001 | Brent put, strike 72 | Jan 2027 | bought 20 000 bbl |\n",
    "| APO-002 | WTI - Brent put, strike -4 | Apr 2027 | sold 15 000 bbl |\n",
    "| APO-003 | HO - Brent crack call, strike 32 | Jun 2027 | sold 25 000 bbl |\n",
    "\n",
    "Every business day the bot prices the book, nets the deltas per underlying (Brent is in all\n",
    "three trades) and holds the opposite in futures. The market is simulated, so the same book can\n",
    "be replayed on many paths with the volatility we choose.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. One simulated path: prices, hedge position\n",
    "2. P&L: options alone vs hedged book\n",
    "3. P&L explain\n",
    "4. Implied vs realised vol, on the crack alone\n",
    "5. Hedge frequency, model and lot rounding"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "7ee2eeb0",
