   "source": [
    "risk = book_risk(book, pricer)\n",
    "print(\"net deltas per underlying, bbl:\", {u: round(d) for u, d in risk.deltas.items()})\n",
    "pd.Series({f\"{u} {m}\": d for (u, m), d in sorted(risk.deltas_by_contract.items())},\n",
    "          name=\"delta bbl\").round(0).to_frame()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9c5d3f00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Brent shows up in all three trades. Added up per underlying, most of it cancels. But a future\n",
    "is an underlying **and** a delivery month, and each fixing uses the front contract of its date:\n",
    "the January Brent put fixes on March Brent, the April spread on June Brent, the June crack on\n",
    "August Brent. Month by month the Brent exposures do not offset, so the bot hedges each contract\n",
    "on its own. The WTI leg of the April spread even splits over two contracts, because May WTI\n",
    "expires on 20 April."
   ]
  },
