  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6b89506",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. P&L explain\n",
    "\n",
    "Every day the option P&L is split with yesterday's greeks:\n",
    "\n",
    "dV ≈ Δ dF + ½ Γ dF² + Θ dt + ν dσ (+ payoffs paid)\n",
    "\n",
    "Γ includes the cross terms between underlyings, which matter for spreads. The delta of the\n",
    "options and the futures P&L almost cancel. What remains is mostly **gamma against theta**:\n",
    "the book is net short options, it collects theta and pays gamma when the market moves."
   ]
  },
