   "source": [
    "Reading the table:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Weekly hedging** trades about half as much but its P&L is much more spread out.\n",
    "- **Kirk is the best of the daily hedges.** The simulated market is lognormal, which is what\n",
    "  Kirk assumes. Bachelier's deltas, built for a normal crack, are off on a 7-month option.\n",
    "- **Whole lots cost precision**: hedging in barrels cuts the spread by about a third. Rounding\n",
    "  each leg on its own can also leave outright exposure when the two deltas differ; rounding in\n",
    "  crack lots first is in the roadmap.\n",
    "\n",
    "With 40 paths the means carry a standard error of about 1 500 to 2 500 $, so compare the\n",
    "spreads rather than the means."
